WEBVTT

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.440
Rebuild an airship?

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.230
Sure, I can do that. Why?

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.200
I'm glad to hear it.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.730
The truth is I would like you 
to win the Black Gathering.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:15.490
Huh?! You're telling me to enter that?

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.730
The Black Gathering?

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.650
It's an airship race.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.400
It's sponsored by a mafia 
alliance and held once a year.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.430
Rumor has it this year's top prize is

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:29.390
the posthumous writings of Isaac Beckford.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.400
My father's?

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.900
It wouldn't be easy to find 
those floating around,

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.250
but if they're real, they could 
offer some clues about him.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:44.840
Yes, and they may even give us an 
idea as to where his laboratory is.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.060
I believe it would be worth 
our while to participate.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.900
There must be some other way to 
get them without entering the race.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.830
Which would mean it's my turn.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:58.010
But...

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:03.020
I hear that Herlock Sholmes 
will be guarding the prize.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.400
All right! We're entering that race!

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.750
You changed your mind fast!

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:14.030
What do we do about an airship, though?

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:15.910
We don't have one.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:19.420
Don't worry. I'll take care of that.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:23.560
It's settled, then. I'm 
counting on you, Impey.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.910
Wow, a race!

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.750
I can't wait to show off 
my genius engineer skills!

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:06.040
Illegal Race

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.030
That Lupin truly is something.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.040
Where did he manage to get this thing?

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:12.550
He said he stole it from
 "a source that will cause us no guilt."

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:17.410
Oh, yeah, that.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.200
Don't worry about it.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.820
Lupin...

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.170
Where's Impey?

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:24.920
I don't see him around.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.870
He's in the workshop.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.190
Apparently he's rebuilding the engine.

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:30.410
I see.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:33.320
We're all gonna be busy 
getting funds together,

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.920
so you'll have to help him out.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:36.730
I'll take care of it.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:41.310
If he tries anything funny, you don't have 
to show any mercy in punishing him.

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:46.070
Van recently taught me an effective kick.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.570
Th-That looks pretty good, all right.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:55.920
I like that smile. Amps up my motivation.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.410
I think your smile looks very good, too!

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.630
Thanks, Drac.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:05.300
Make the walls thicker to 
increase air pressure...

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:09.060
No, I might as well overhaul 
the whole control system...

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.120
Impey, sorry to interrupt.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:13.450
Um...

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.560
These sandwiches are amazing!

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:23.640
Delicious!

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:24.810
I'm glad.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:27.230
I didn't do a very good job making them.

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:28.820
No, they're great!

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.940
Is the rebuild going well?

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.900
I've been trying a lot of stuff,

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:38.770
but it's still not quite enough horsepower.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.590
I'll handle it, though. Leave it to me.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:45.970
After all, I'm the man who's 
gonna go to the moon someday!

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:47.940
You said that before, too.

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.510
But you mean... <i>the</i> moon?

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:52.480
Yeah! <i>The</i> moon!

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.100
It's my dream!

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:58.090
It all started with a steam engine.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.100
The first time I saw one,

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.030
I thought it was so cool.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:05.890
It was enough to change my whole world.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.810
I wanted to make things like that, too.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.830
Of course, it didn't work 
out so well at first.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:18.380
My master... or teacher, 
whatever you'd call him...

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.370
He told me something.

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:23.840
"Science is the power that makes 
the impossible possible."

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.190
"It's the dreams and hopes of all people."

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:28.460
"It can even take you to the moon."

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:33.090
I was so excited. I mean, it's the moon!

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:37.450
If I could pull it off, anyone who 
saw me would think it was amazing!

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:38.940
Just like I did as a kid!

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:41.920
That's why I'm gonna go to the moon.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:45.640
To prove that science is all 
of our hopes and dreams.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:49.600
Everyone made fun of me, 
saying that was ridiculous.

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:52.890
I'm serious, though.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:57.740
So a little rebuild like this is nothing!

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:02.140
I'll win that race, no matter what! 
For your sake too, Cardia!

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:12.220
Ugh, Impey... Give me a break!

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:15.370
Who knew he could be so absent-minded?

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.850
This is beyond my expectations.

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:22.930
This is the top Asian style 
of apology: the kneeling bow!

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:25.600
I'm sorry. The rebuild isn't done yet.

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:28.920
Isn't the race about to start?

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.560
Is he gonna make it?

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:35.450
Who can say? Punctuality 
certainly isn't his strong suit.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:39.210
C-Count, how can you sound so unconcerned?

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:41.850
Impey...

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.870
W-We mustn't get nervous.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:46.200
I know Impey will be here soon...

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:50.090
Sorry for the wait!

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:52.970
The star of the show is here!

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:56.470
Impey! You had me worried!

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.340
What do you think? That's ol' Impey for ya!

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.700
I'm a man who keeps his promises!

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:09.240
Yeah, yeah. Come on, 
let's start getting ready.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:12.290
If you'd been any later,
 I'd have shot you full of lead.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:16.240
Jeez, you guys are cold! 
You could be a little more sympathetic.

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:20.010
My... How wonderful!

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:23.240
What a truly wonderful ship!

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:26.000
Really? You understand my ship?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.570
I do! Of course I do!

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:31.960
I am the scientist who will one day 
expose the truth of this world!

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:34.710
My name is... Nemo!

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:36.020
And now you know.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:37.300
Uh...

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:41.410
W-Well, I don't really get you...

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:45.220
But just look at this functional beauty!

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:47.310
Just like a young maiden, isn't it?

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:49.370
Yes, I get it! Of course I do!

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:52.580
Like a bashful girl in love!

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.830
Nemo?

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.150
Yes, Nemo.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:55.520
What's up?

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:57.470
Well, just...

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:00.580
I know him, actually.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:06.530
When I was part of the Royal Society, 
he declared me his rival.

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:10.780
Ah, so you're saying 
he's quite the nuisance.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.520
Very good!

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:16.550
It was surely fate that led me to meet 
a wonderful fellow scientist here!

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:22.130
Allow me to give you a special tour 
of my prototype airship, the Fulton!

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:24.520
I'm in! Wait, prototype?

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.940
Yes, of course!

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:31.340
One day, I will create the wonder 
battle airship Nautilus!

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:30.240
Hey, he's leaving with him!

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:31.400
That's okay.

00:08:32.350 --> 00:08:34.870
I can get it ready to fly.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.260
Has everyone finished their checks?

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:40.910
Observation deck, clear.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:43.300
Main deck, clear.

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:45.930
The engine room's clear, too.

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:50.100
Oh? You're doing a fine job as captain.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:53.730
Impey, all the flight 
preparations are complete.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:55.390
Everything is clear.

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:59.800
Okay. I just got us an aether transmitter.

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:03.340
What was that man's... Nemo's ship like?

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:06.440
Well... It was impressive, all right.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:09.970
Of course, we're still 
going to win, though.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:11.560
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:14.300
The long wait is now over!

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:18.590
The Black Gathering race is about to begin!

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:20.390
Make sure you win!

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:24.070
We fly along the Thames,

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:25.880
turn around when we reach Big Ben,

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:28.210
and fly back here. That's the course.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.470
I'll be counting on your guidance.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:31.830
Leave it to me.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:33.940
Start us off at full throttle!

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:36.590
We shoot straight up until we reach altitude!

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:37.960
Roger.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:51.110
Three!

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.100
Two!

00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:53.350
One!

00:09:53.350 --> 00:09:54.600
Start!

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:00.130
The race has finally begun!

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:04.110
Jumping into an early lead is the 
rookie ship flying its first race,

00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:07.130
the Impey, Princess, and Henchmen!

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:10.460
Hey! I heard that, Impey! 
Who are you calling henchmen?!

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.460
Don't get so mad.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:14.420
It's just a little playful spirit.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:17.120
I suppose I would have to 
say that's just like you.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:22.800
Uh, that name is too long, so I'll just 
call it the Princess and Henchmen.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:25.270
Hey! The most important part's gone!

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.650
Ship approaching at eight o'clock!

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:30.980
It's gonna ram us!

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:36.130
The Purple Lightning Sky Pirate attacks!

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:38.790
An intense battle has begun!

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:41.290
Fran! Increase engine speed!

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.770
Roger!

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:47.790
Good! That's it!

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:51.910
But with no guns, we have no way to attack.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:54.640
Yeah, I got rid of them 
to reduce our weight.

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.410
At any rate, to flee is to win!

00:10:56.410 --> 00:10:59.770
All right, if we just 
stay in first place...

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:03.780
Impey, we've got trouble! 
The paint's flaking off!

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:06.980
The paint? Like that even matters.

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:08.660
It does matter!

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:11.930
Hey, isn't that our ship?

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:14.480
That emblem... It's definitely ours!

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:17.940
Oh, dear! Now this is
 a shocking development!

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:21.820
It's been discovered that the Princess 
and Henchmen is a ship stolen

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:23.740
from the Adele and Brutus Firm!

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:28.530
Word has it there's a cash reward of 
20 million for whoever shoots it down!

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:33.200
So the "source that will cause us no guilt" 
Lupin mentioned was...

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:34.910
The bookie?

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:38.150
If you had to steal it, couldn't you 
have stolen it from somewhere else?

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:40.310
Well, they know now! 
There's no changing that!

00:11:40.310 --> 00:11:42.340
More importantly,
 they're coming up behind us!

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.190
Behind us?

00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:46.230
No way!

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:48.470
There's no way they could 
catch up to this ship!

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:52.490
They're prepared to self-destruct...

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:56.020
They're so blinded by the reward money, 
they've abandoned the race!

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:00.480
The Princess and Henchmen is hit!

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:02.740
Status report!

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:04.790
The lower armor took a hit.

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:06.230
Looks like there's a hole.

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:08.490
Air pump 12 is damaged.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:11.740
Expelling ballast water to 
regulate our buoyancy.

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:14.760
Damn you!

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:18.760
It's dodging! The Princess and 
Henchmen is certainly tenacious!

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:21.510
It's dodging the concentrated fire
 with skillful maneuvering!

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:27.040
But with this many of them surrounding us,
 we'll be caught eventually.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:37.490
Impey!

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:38.770
Something's coming!

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:46.290
They helped us?

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:48.740
No, that's...

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:53.280
Impey Barbicane... Your ship is wonderful.

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:57.630
However, the Fulton is going to win!

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:14.340
Impey Barbicane... Your ship is wonderful.

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:18.780
However the Fulton is going to win!

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:26.320
Behold, my ingenious technical prowess!

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:38.090
There is no escape from the Fulton!

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:40.840
Impey!

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.850
It's the turn-around point! 
Shake him off here!

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:45.410
Oh, damn it!

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:48.350
Fran! Crank the engine up to the red zone!

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:50.590
Red zone! Okay!

00:13:56.470 --> 00:13:58.240
What?!

00:13:58.480 --> 00:13:59.370
Yes!

00:13:59.370 --> 00:14:01.510
Impey! In front of us!

00:14:01.510 --> 00:14:03.100
What now?

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:05.740
Huh?!

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:07.100
You're kidding me!

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:10.680
They knew they couldn't 
catch us on the first leg,

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.030
so they ambushed us on the return trip.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:19.890
The Princess and Henchmen

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:21.640
is forced to hide in the clouds!

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:23.390
It's taken a lot of damage!

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:25.120
The engine's hit!

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:26.640
One engine's down!

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:27.880
Air pump damaged.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:30.130
If we lose one more, we're going down!

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:32.880
What do we do, Impey?

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:35.140
We have to do something about them!

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:39.000
I thought this might happen!

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:45.100
Hey, what is this?

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:48.480
This ship's greatest, most 
powerful secret weapon!

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:52.370
Cardia, prepare to counterattack.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:55.860
Got it.

00:14:57.280 --> 00:15:00.130
Cardia, your orders, please.

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:06.890
First, follow these steps 
to put Van in the capsule.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:09.950
What did you say you were gonna do to me?

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:12.820
Hey! Hey!

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:15.270
Who do you think I am?! Let me out!

00:15:13.460 --> 00:15:15.270
All set.

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:17.010
Is this...

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:17.010
Hey!

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:18.010
Yep!

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:21.710
Time for Impey's Special Helsing Cannon!

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:28.020
Here we go!

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:29.420
Prepare to fire!

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:30.780
Three!

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:31.820
Two!

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:32.920
One!

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:34.770
Blast the hell out of 'em!

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:35.940
But...

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:38.340
And push.

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:49.180
Van!

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:51.660
Go as wild on 'em as you want!

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:56.140
Impey, I'll make you regret that later!

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:20.170
Wh-What is happening?

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:25.330
One of the Princess and Henchmen's crew 
is taking over an enemy ship on foot!

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:28.830
Impey! The big one's coming!

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:29.830
Roger!

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:37.840
Oh, my! The Fulton has caught up 
and resumed its vicious attack!

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:41.000
You won't get away!

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:47.230
The Fulton will be the winner!

00:16:58.610 --> 00:17:00.110
What?!

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:03.390
I'm sick of that damn laugh of yours.

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:13.000
The Fulton is conquered.

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:17.880
Van!

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:28.460
I may have lost this time,

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:33.390
but I will someday face you in battle again!

00:17:33.390 --> 00:17:36.200
I'll be back!

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:40.090
The Fulton has exploded!

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.840
E-Exploded?! What about Van?!

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:45.410
No worries! He's on his way back now!

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:51.340
Van, are you all right?

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.430
N-No problem.

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:56.270
I'm fine. You need to head back.

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:57.820
R-Right.

00:17:58.630 --> 00:18:02.470
Impey, you know what's coming, don't you?

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:03.920
Yikes, I'm scared!

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.090
Welcome back, Cardia.

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:07.900
Thanks, I'm—

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:12.500
Uh-oh! The Princess and Henchmen 
is starting to fall!

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:15.440
Is it going to crash?!

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:18.050
Fran?!

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:20.940
Um, I have news.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:24.360
The engine has completely overheated.

00:18:24.360 --> 00:18:25.450
In other words...

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:27.240
Yeah, we're going down.

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:30.950
Going down?

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:33.310
Will they reach the goal or crash first?!

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.980
They're in an endless dead heat with death!

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:37.980
Fine by me!

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:41.960
I'm all for a dynamic, 
dramatic emergency landing!

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:43.150
Impey...

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:47.730
I do still intend to reach the goal, 
but I'll apologize in advance.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:51.470
Well, Impey does usually manage 
to pull it off when it counts.

00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:52.660
True.

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:56.370
Isn't a bit of thrill a good thing?

00:18:58.790 --> 00:18:59.910
It'll be okay.

00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:02.430
You can do it, Impey.

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:03.530
You can reach the goal...

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.810
and go to the moon.

00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:10.720
Thanks, Cardia!

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:13.740
Those words give me the 
strength of a hundred men!

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:18.380
Go!

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:21.760
Impey! You're nearly at the goal!

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:26.780
Go!

00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:41.210
With Impey's skills on your side,
 you're sure to win!

00:19:42.270 --> 00:19:44.890
You liar. We nearly died.

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:49.780
But the airship broke. 
Will things be all right?

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:53.390
With all these unexpected developments, 
the gamblers had a field day.

00:19:53.390 --> 00:19:55.580
I'm sure the sponsors made a nice profit.

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:58.520
They're placing no blame this time.

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:01.980
That was terribly reckless, you know?

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:04.140
Still...

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:09.430
This brings us one step closer 
to your dream, Cardia.

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:14.640
My dream?

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:18.440
Yeah! We'll start by getting rid 
of the poison in your body!

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:21.480
Thanks, Impey.

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:27.610
Enjoying yourself, eh?

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:34.580
Yes, I am.

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:37.820
Now, let's take a picture of our winners.

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:39.080
Squeeze together.

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:41.740
Come on, Drac. You and 
Sisi get in this, too.

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:44.080
Sh-Should I stand here?

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:47.280
You, the young man with 
glasses! Smile for me!

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:49.100
You're frowning!

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:51.590
He sure told you.

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:56.280
<i>When we're together, I have fun.</i>

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:00.070
<i>When we're together, 
it makes me want to dream.</i>

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:03.050
<i>No matter what happens from now on,</i>

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.280
<i>I know that this day...</i>

00:21:06.340 --> 00:21:08.120
All right, here we go!

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:10.860
Watch the birdie!

00:21:12.570 --> 00:21:17.060
<i>...will be a precious memory for me.</i>

00:23:01.210 --> 00:23:04.460
This... is Isaac's lab?

00:23:14.750 --> 00:23:18.510
Why don't you stop pretending to be human?

00:23:21.310 --> 00:23:22.450
Are these...

00:23:26.990 --> 00:23:28.520
Homunculus?

00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:33.000
After all, my sister, you are truly...

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:37.570
a monster.
